description:
NECTURE empowers businesses to unlock the full potential of fleets, seamlessly bridging the gap between mobility and energy. Combining human\-driven information with data\-driven intelligence, we provide tailored solutions that optimize operations, reduce costs, and achieve sustainability goals. NECTURE is building a world where electric fleets are not only possible, but thrive.






 With a growing number of customers around the world, and an exciting data\-driven product that is developing continuously, we are looking for a
 **Data Scientist (full\-time)** 
 to join our team asap within Austria or in a hybrid/remote setup (details to be discussed individually).





 Tasks



* Lead development of ML models powering forecasting and optimization;

* Handling and analyzing geospatial data related to our products;

* Developing \& reviewing spatio\-temporal models;

* Build production\-grade ML pipelines, monitoring, and deployment processes;

* Collaborate with backend and product teams to integrate ML at scale;

* Advocating Data Science topics to other members of the team.





 Requirements



* 2–4 years experience as Data Scientist/ML Engineer;

* Strong applied ML skills (Python, ML frameworks, MLOps tools);

* Experience in deploying/maintaining models in production;

* Experience in working in dynamic environments (e.g. Startup/scale\-up);

* Solid communication skills with engineers, PMs, leadership;

* Good English language skills (German language not required);






**Nice\-to\-have:** 
 experience with Azure ML tools \& Kedro.





 Benefits



* Opportunity to contribute and grow in high\-performing, cross\-functional teams in a people\-first culture.

* Fast\-paced setup with autonomy, creative freedom, and the opportunity to drive real impact.

* A work environment that values experimentation, adaptability, continuous learning, and team well\-being (e.g. options of working reduced hours or hybrid setups).

* Emphasis on results over facetime, promoting flexibility, care, and balance.

* Regular team events, English as working language and great equipment.

* Receive a competitive salary based on your experience and qualifications.






 As an innovative start\-up, we value your fresh ideas, unique perspectives, and motivations to contribute to a livable future with the power of climate tech.
